## TO COPY A FILE FROM A DIFFERENT SERVER

`curl -fL -o bakar-key.pem https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kcommit/shell-scripting/main/bakar-key.pem` (This is used to download a file from a website, downloading a private key here for a AWS machine)
`chmod 400 bakar-key.pem` (bakar-key.pem is the name of the key, private keys wont work with too open permissions)
`ssh -i bakar-key.pem ubuntu@18.117.82.220` (optional if you want to enter the machine, ubuntu is the username and after @ is the public ip)
` scp -r -i bakar-key.pem ubuntu@18.117.82.220:/home/ubuntu/shell-scripting /home/ibrahim` (after the ip is the location of the file we need to copy, and at the end is the location we want to copy the file to)
(-i is used to enter with a private key, -r is used to copy directories)

## TO COPY A FILE TO THE SERVER

`scp -r -i bakar-key-pem /home/ibrahim/folder ubuntu@18.117.82.220:/home/ubuntu`(/home/ibrahim/folder is the path of the folder we want to copy, and after that is the user, ip and the path we want to copy the folder to)